"context": "The headline covers the 213 current voting House Democrats. Nearly all have said nothing on the record, which scores 0 and holds both averages near zero. Most of the public hesitation comes from incoming members, shown as their own group below. Unlike the Senate's secret ballot, the speaker is chosen in a public floor vote on Jan. 3 and needs a majority of the whole House.",
"method": [
"Scale: +5 repeated vocal advocacy; +4 explicit endorsement with a stated reason; +3 says they will support him; +2 defends his record or leadership; +1 mild positive signal; 0 no statement found; -1 declines to commit when asked; -2 calls for new leadership or a leadership debate without ruling him out; -3 withholds support and sets conditions; -4 says it is time for new leadership, backs someone else or says their vote is currently no; -5 flatly says they will not support him.",
"Scores are one reader's judgment of public statements reported in the press. They are not vote predictions.",
"Weight = 1 + 9 x (years in the House as of January 2027) / 46. The longest-serving member gets 10 and a new member gets 1.",
"Jeffries himself and the non-voting delegates are left out.",
"Incoming members are listed only once they have said something on the record, so they are kept out of the headline figure: the full freshman class is not final while races are still being called. Their group average therefore covers only those who have spoken.",
"The roster is the current House Democratic caucus. It does not yet mark members who are retiring or lost, and who will not vote for speaker in January.",
"A score of 0 means nothing was found on the record, not that the member is neutral. Many are allies who have simply not been quoted."
],
